1
00:00:00,994 --> 00:00:02,151
Welcome to Lumen.

2
00:00:02,151 --> 00:00:05,623
A friendly chat workspace, built on GitHub Copilot.

3
00:00:05,959 --> 00:00:09,538
You may already chat with GitHub Copilot in VS Code.

4
00:00:09,538 --> 00:00:13,873
Behind the scenes, that chat now runs on the Copilot CLI agent.

5
00:00:13,873 --> 00:00:17,796
It reads your files, uses tools, and gets real work done.

6
00:00:17,796 --> 00:00:24,541
But VS Code is built around code, and most of the team works in plans, spreadsheets and documents.

7
00:00:24,883 --> 00:00:31,733
Lumen runs on that same Copilot agent, in a chat window built for that kind of work, on your own computer.

8
00:00:31,733 --> 00:00:35,933
And yes, if Claude Code is what you have, Lumen runs on that too.

9
00:00:36,191 --> 00:00:40,372
In the next few minutes, you'll learn how to use every part of it, step by step.

10
00:00:40,667 --> 00:00:41,330
Step one.

11
00:00:41,330 --> 00:00:42,139
Get set up.

12
00:00:44,193 --> 00:00:47,163
The first time you open Lumen, it asks three things.

13
00:00:47,163 --> 00:00:47,735
Your name,

14
00:00:50,924 --> 00:00:52,448
which AI engine to use.

15
00:00:52,448 --> 00:00:56,556
GitHub Copilot is ready, and Claude Code sits right beside it,

16
00:00:59,851 --> 00:01:01,755
and where your work lives.

17
00:01:01,755 --> 00:01:03,878
That folder is your notebook.

18
00:01:03,878 --> 00:01:09,515
Keep it in OneDrive, and Microsoft 365 Copilot can find the same files later.

19
00:01:13,441 --> 00:01:14,023
Step two.

20
00:01:14,023 --> 00:01:15,382
Find your way around.

21
00:01:17,434 --> 00:01:22,278
If you've used Microsoft 365 Copilot, this will feel familiar.

22
00:01:22,278 --> 00:01:23,684
That's on purpose.

23
00:01:25,677 --> 00:01:27,226
The same rail on the left.

24
00:01:27,226 --> 00:01:29,670
Chat, Agents, Prompts, and your Notebook.

25
00:01:29,670 --> 00:01:36,941
The same words, and the same habits, so everything you learn here carries straight over when your Copilot licence arrives.

26
00:01:38,931 --> 00:01:45,523
And so nobody mixes them up, every message box says plainly which tool you're in, and which engine is answering.

27
00:01:46,591 --> 00:01:47,248
Step three.

28
00:01:47,248 --> 00:01:48,383
Chat with an agent.

29
00:01:49,334 --> 00:01:50,671
Agents are specialists.

30
00:01:50,671 --> 00:01:55,670
Pick one, like the Requirements Coach, and it offers starter prompts to get you going.

31
00:01:57,498 --> 00:02:00,385
Under the message box, choose what Lumen may do.

32
00:02:00,385 --> 00:02:03,512
Just chat, read your files, or create and edit them.

33
00:02:03,512 --> 00:02:06,458
And pick a response mode, from quick to thorough.

34
00:02:08,119 --> 00:02:11,981
Send it, and the answer streams in, with real headings and tables.

35
00:02:17,825 --> 00:02:24,652
User stories, Given, When, Then acceptance criteria, and the open questions to take back to the business.

36
00:02:25,833 --> 00:02:26,473
Step four.

37
00:02:26,473 --> 00:02:27,753
Work with the reply.

38
00:02:30,629 --> 00:02:32,275
Lumen suggests a next step.

39
00:02:32,275 --> 00:02:35,749
Click it to send, or press the up arrow to edit it first.

40
00:02:38,527 --> 00:02:42,623
Every reply can be copied, retried, or branched into a new chat.

41
00:02:42,623 --> 00:02:45,823
A thumbs up or down tells the team what's working.

42
00:02:46,695 --> 00:02:47,713
Need a document?

43
00:02:47,713 --> 00:02:49,112
Export, Word document.

44
00:02:49,112 --> 00:02:53,437
Real headings, lists, and tables, saved straight into your notebook.

45
00:02:56,861 --> 00:03:02,024
Your own messages can be edited and resent, or saved as a prompt to reuse any time.

46
00:03:03,006 --> 00:03:03,611
Step five.

47
00:03:03,611 --> 00:03:04,820
Bring in your files.

48
00:03:09,571 --> 00:03:14,024
To practise, the home screen sets up a sample project in one click.

49
00:03:14,024 --> 00:03:18,809
A Microsoft Project plan, with a budget, risks, and timesheets in Excel.

50
00:03:23,007 --> 00:03:26,207
Open the Notebook to see everything in your project folder.

51
00:03:33,796 --> 00:03:41,220
To use a file in a chat, type a slash, exactly like in Microsoft 365 Copilot, and pick it.

52
00:03:42,200 --> 00:03:46,232
Lumen reads the real plan, and you can watch every step as it works.

53
00:03:52,668 --> 00:03:53,280
Step six.

54
00:03:53,280 --> 00:03:54,844
Use the prompt gallery.

55
00:03:58,747 --> 00:04:03,957
Saved prompts ask a few simple questions, then hand the work to the right agent.

56
00:04:03,957 --> 00:04:08,581
Project plans, budgets, the delivery lifecycle, Azure DevOps, and more.

57
00:04:12,820 --> 00:04:14,512
Open the project health check.

58
00:04:14,512 --> 00:04:17,840
Lumen has already picked the right plan from your notebook.

59
00:04:17,840 --> 00:04:18,516
Click Start.

60
00:04:32,030 --> 00:04:37,939
Red, amber or green, the critical path, slippage against the baseline, and who's over allocated.

61
00:04:38,909 --> 00:04:41,917
And any table copies straight into Excel or Outlook.

62
00:04:42,177 --> 00:04:42,940
Step seven.

63
00:04:42,940 --> 00:04:44,119
Put it on repeat.

64
00:04:49,097 --> 00:04:51,627
Open the prompt again, and choose Repeat.

65
00:04:51,627 --> 00:04:53,108
Weekly, Mondays at nine.

66
00:04:59,023 --> 00:05:01,222
Scheduled prompts get their own tab.

67
00:05:01,222 --> 00:05:06,169
Lumen runs them while it's open, and leaves the result waiting as an unread chat.

68
00:05:07,179 --> 00:05:07,858
Step eight.

69
00:05:07,858 --> 00:05:10,081
Let Lumen update your files, safely.

70
00:05:16,525 --> 00:05:22,114
Update the plan reads this week's progress workbook, and applies it to the Microsoft Project plan.

71
00:05:23,726 --> 00:05:25,604
It never touches the original.

72
00:05:25,604 --> 00:05:30,361
It saves an updated copy, checks the schedule again, and lists every change.

73
00:05:40,218 --> 00:05:44,783
See changes shows exactly what moved, task by task, before and after.

74
00:05:47,508 --> 00:05:51,289
To create new files, switch the chat to Create and edit files.

75
00:05:51,289 --> 00:05:53,972
Ask for an Excel tracker with a Gantt chart,

76
00:05:56,686 --> 00:06:00,078
and there it is, colour coded and ready for the steering committee.

77
00:06:02,210 --> 00:06:02,864
Step nine.

78
00:06:02,864 --> 00:06:04,301
Create your own agent.

79
00:06:09,147 --> 00:06:12,369
Describe what you need in one sentence, and click Draft it.

80
00:06:17,189 --> 00:06:22,644
Lumen fills in the same fields as Agent Builder in Microsoft 365 Copilot.

81
00:06:22,644 --> 00:06:26,605
Name, description, instructions, and starter prompts.

82
00:06:26,605 --> 00:06:29,819
It even switches on the right capabilities.

83
00:06:33,304 --> 00:06:38,318
Anything marked Lumen only runs on this computer, so you always know what will carry over.

84
00:06:40,545 --> 00:06:43,084
Create it, and pin your favourites to the sidebar.

85
00:06:50,699 --> 00:06:51,403
Step ten.

86
00:06:51,403 --> 00:06:53,046
Connect Azure DevOps.

87
00:06:58,675 --> 00:07:02,814
In Settings, under Connections, paste your organisation's address.

88
00:07:02,814 --> 00:07:08,019
Lumen signs in with your Azure account, or an access token that it keeps encrypted.

89
00:07:08,283 --> 00:07:12,507
Check the connection, then pick the project, the team, and the wikis to search.

90
00:07:17,648 --> 00:07:22,832
Now agents like the Backlog Helper can search and read your work items and wiki pages.

91
00:07:34,955 --> 00:07:38,699
And when an agent wants to change something, it only proposes.

92
00:07:38,699 --> 00:07:41,355
Switch the chat to Create and edit, and ask.

93
00:07:54,925 --> 00:07:59,106
The change arrives as an approval card, showing exactly what will be written.

94
00:07:59,381 --> 00:08:02,480
Nothing reaches Azure DevOps until you click Apply.

95
00:08:02,480 --> 00:08:07,039
Lumen checks that nobody changed it in the meantime, and records your name.

96
00:08:08,019 --> 00:08:08,845
Step eleven.

97
00:08:08,845 --> 00:08:11,048
Run a guided delivery lifecycle.

98
00:08:20,014 --> 00:08:23,285
The lifecycle sample sets up a program's documents.

99
00:08:23,285 --> 00:08:30,404
Requirements and a project definition in Word, a solution blueprint, a data model, and a traceability workbook.

100
00:08:36,103 --> 00:08:40,434
The traceability check reads every layer, from business requirement to story.

101
00:08:49,492 --> 00:08:55,583
Coverage for every layer, stories that would build the wrong thing, broken links, and conflicting sources.

102
00:08:55,583 --> 00:08:58,111
Each one with a cell reference and an owner.

103
00:09:03,512 --> 00:09:05,985
For bigger work, start a lifecycle run.

104
00:09:05,985 --> 00:09:12,707
Requirements, functional design, technical design, and stories, with an approval gate between every stage.

105
00:09:12,961 --> 00:09:16,938
Name the run, choose the source documents, and start the first stage.

106
00:09:16,938 --> 00:09:21,089
Each stage works in its own chat, and saves its output to your notebook.

107
00:09:48,783 --> 00:09:52,343
Before you sign off, run an advisory traceability check.

108
00:09:52,343 --> 00:09:55,012
It reports gaps, and never changes a file.

109
00:10:10,071 --> 00:10:10,902
Then approve.

110
00:10:10,902 --> 00:10:15,821
Your name and the time are stamped on the output, and the next stage unlocks.

111
00:10:15,821 --> 00:10:22,594
With Azure DevOps connected, an approved stage publishes to the wiki, or becomes work items, in one click.

112
00:10:23,483 --> 00:10:24,176
Step twelve.

113
00:10:24,176 --> 00:10:25,275
See what's working.

114
00:10:29,132 --> 00:10:33,335
Every thumbs up and down lands in Insights, by agent and by prompt.

115
00:10:33,335 --> 00:10:35,468
And it all stays on this computer.

116
00:10:36,349 --> 00:10:37,703
Step thirteen.

117
00:10:37,703 --> 00:10:40,893
Take it to Microsoft 365 Copilot.

118
00:10:47,769 --> 00:10:51,211
When your Copilot licence arrives, export any agent.

119
00:10:51,211 --> 00:10:56,110
Paste it straight into Agent Builder, or hand IT a ready made app package.

120
00:11:00,106 --> 00:11:05,269
Your prompts export too, as plain text, ready to save in Copilot's prompt gallery.

121
00:11:09,219 --> 00:11:16,217
And every agent and skill exports into VS Code, so it works in GitHub Copilot Chat and Claude Code too.

122
00:11:18,331 --> 00:11:19,291
Step fourteen.

123
00:11:19,291 --> 00:11:20,251
Make it yours.

124
00:11:24,260 --> 00:11:25,487
Lumen is pluggable.

125
00:11:25,487 --> 00:11:30,980
It runs on GitHub Copilot, or on Claude Code, and switching is one click in Settings.

126
00:11:31,840 --> 00:11:33,419
Light or dark, your choice.

127
00:11:37,438 --> 00:11:40,510
And press control slash, for every keyboard shortcut.

128
00:11:43,764 --> 00:11:44,241
Lumen.

129
00:11:44,241 --> 00:11:51,956
Built for GitHub Copilot, ready for Microsoft 365 Copilot, and friendly for everyone on the team.
